# ARKA HelpDesk — Project Context

ARKA HelpDesk is a lightweight ticket + knowledge-base system serving all of Iwan's apps (MineOps, Sarang ERP, ArkFleet, VASIA POS, Pratasaba Resort). Users submit issues via Telegram Bot → AI auto-reply (GPT-4o Mini via OpenRouter) searches KB → unresolved tickets escalate via DM to Iwan. Web dashboard for Iwan to manage tickets.

**Tech Stack:** Laravel 13 (PHP 8.3+) + React 19 + Inertia.js 2.x + Ant Design 5.x
**Database:** MySQL 8.4 (Docker)
**Queue:** Laravel Queue (Redis driver)
**AI:** OpenRouter → `openai/gpt-4o-mini` ($0.15/$0.60 per 1M in/out)
**Search:** MySQL FULLTEXT on `kb_articles` table
**Deploy:** Docker Compose on IDCloudHost VPS (103.55.38.96), Nginx port 82
**Testing:** Browser Automation at `http://localhost:8000` (assume server already running)

## Ticket Lifecycle (6 states)
`open` → `ai_replied` → `escalated` → `in_progress` → `resolved` → `closed`

## Database Tables
- `users` — super_admin, admin (Iwan), user roles; linked to Telegram via telegram_id
- `apps` — registered applications (mineops, sarang-erp, arkfleet, pos-atk, pratasaba-resort)
- `tickets` — core entity: user_id, app_id, assigned_to, subject, status, priority, source (telegram/web), kb_match_id, metadata (JSON)
- `ticket_messages` — polymorphic sender (user/ai/admin), is_ai_generated flag, kb_article_id ref
- `kb_articles` — title, content (TEXT), tags (JSON), FULLTEXT index, view_count, helpful_count
- `kb_article_links` — related article graph (article_id → related_article_id with link_type)
- `ai_conversations` — ticket_id FK, prompt (JSON), response (TEXT), tokens_used, model, cost
- `telegram_sessions` — user state machine (JSON), chat_id, last_activity_at

## Priority Levels
`low`, `medium`, `high`, `critical`

